# Agent discipline (NavBot)

## Do not change behavior unless asked

- Only implement what the user explicitly requested in the current task.
- Do **not** add runtime fixes, refactors, logging, or "helpful" extras on your own.
- If the user said **build once at path time** (e.g. `ProcessAreaPath`, apex list), do **not** reintroduce per-tick/per-frame reprocessing of that logic (no runtime center forcing, no `GetMovementTarget` rebuilding paths).
- When intent is unclear or multiple approaches exist, **ask a short clarifying question** before coding. Do not guess.

## Lmaobox API — MCP first, never hallucinate

Before using any Lmaobox/game API (entity methods, props, flags, callbacks, engine/draw):

1. Use **`user-lmaobox-context`** MCP:
   - `get_smart_context("<Symbol>")` — signatures, examples, gotchas
   - `get_types("<Symbol>")` — type/signature check
   - `smart_search("<topic>")` — find correct symbol name
   - `traceback` — map bundled `NavBot.lua` line numbers to source modules
2. If MCP has **no definition**, do not invent the API. Use documented alternatives (e.g. `m_fFlags & FL_ONGROUND`, not `Entity:IsOnGround()` unless MCP confirms it).
3. Prefer `lmaobox_lua_documentation.md` in repo root as secondary reference; MCP wins on conflicts.

## NavBot navigation invariants (do not break without explicit request)

| Concern                     | Build time (once)                          | Runtime (per tick)                                            |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| String-pull / center apexes | `PathStringPull.ProcessAreaPath`           | Walk `G.Navigation.apexPath` only                             |
| Door portals for steering   | `STRING_PULL_DOORS_ONLY` in string-pull    | —                                                             |
| Pop path[1]                 | —                                          | `CanAdvanceToNext`: in path[2] OR `CanSkip` to path[2] only   |
| Draw / visuals              | Read cached `apexPath`, `currentTargetPos` | Never call `GetMovementTarget` or `ProcessAreaPath` in `Draw` |

## When stuck

State what you are unsure about and ask. A wrong confident change is worse than one question.

## Design over edge cases

- Prefer one rule that holds everywhere (e.g. portal shared-axis tolerance, segment pass = entered next area) over per-situation hacks.
- Build-time geometry (approach points along portal line, portal spans) must match runtime checks — same constants, same definitions.
- Never target nav area geometric center for movement; waypoints are portal openings and goals only.
- Segment exit direction comes from the **connection graph** (`GetExitDirToNeighbor`), not center-to-center rays.
- Area containment Z uses **local floor** on the nav quad with `NodeTouchHeight` (82) — not flat min-corner Z.
- Hot-path state (`apexIndex`, movement target) advances at most once per tick; no unbounded loops in CreateMove.
- **No legacy "just in case"** — delete dead code when rewriting; do not keep parallel systems (waypoints + apex, STUCK state, pathHistory).
- Shared 2D math lives in `NavBot.Utils.NavMath` (or `Common`); never duplicate `horizontalDir` / portal axis helpers per file.
- `ProcessAreaPath` only at path-find; runtime uses `ConsumeNodeApexes` + `UpdateGoalApex`.
- Pop path[1] via `CanAdvanceToNext`: strict `in_next_area`, portal edge pass (not center), or `CanSkip` to path[2] only while on path[1] (touch/portal band).
- `AlignPathIfDesynced` only when feet are on path[i] i>1 but path[1] is stale (recovery, not every-tick sync).
- Apex steering clamped to current segment (path[1]->path[2]); never skip apexes ahead while path[1] remains.
- String-pull build: same wall enter+exit on an area → `same_side_center` apex before portal.
- Z drop > STEP_HEIGHT between areas → `drop` apex; segment passes on airborne/landed, not geometric skip.
- Repath start: `GetPathStartNode` (area-at-feet); after A\* `AlignPathPrefixToPlayer` trims stale prefix.
- Drop apex steering: nearest portal span point; walk-off nudge when near edge. No portal_overshoot on drops/jumps.
- SmartJump runs once per tick from `MovementDecisions` only; sim uses `apexPath` at current speed.
